<title>UK: BPB down as SBC Warburg cuts to &quot;hold&quot;.</title>
<headline>BPB down as SBC Warburg cuts to &quot;hold&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in plasterboard maker BPB Plc dropped on Tuesday as analysts at SBC Warburg cut the stock to &quot;hold&quot; from &quot;buy&quot; and lowered earnings estimates to reflect the impact of the recent strength of sterling, dealers said.  </p>
<p>The stock was down 7p at 367-1/2 by 1057 GMT in volume of just over two million shares.</p>
<p>Analysts at Warburg were not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>BPB shares have been stuck in a range broadly between 340p and 380p since last August.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
